      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The passage presents Plate IV as a numbered set of facial painting designs.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Items 1-4 depict the dorsal fin of Wasx and the back, dorsal fin, or short bear's tail of the sea-monster Ts’an xd’utsé.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Items 5-8 describe designs whose lips represent the mouth of a sculpin, with added spines, vertebrae, or flippers.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Other designs represent a raven's hat, mountain-goat horns or ears, whale eyes, a sea-monster's hat and ears, bear feet and ears, a devil-fish nose, sea-lion teeth, and a killer whale's throat.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3",
        "ev:4",
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Many entries assign the designs to named groups with formulas such as 'Used by ...'.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1",
        "ev:2",
        "ev:3",
        "ev:4",
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Several entries specify colors, especially red, black, and blue, and some specify positions on the face such as lips, over the mouth, nose, forehead, eyebrows, and chin.",
