    "summary": "The passage closes a prior account by saying a ritual stone was lost when its keeper dropped it to prevent capture, but the ceremony continued among priests and through Animal-Boy's descendants. It then introduces the Stone-Medicine-Men and explains that the altar object thought by outsiders to be a white stone was understood by initiates as a giant's thigh bone, discovered after a hunter dreamed at Swimming-Mound of a large being who said drowned people's bones there held curative power.",
