      "text": "A man becomes separated from his war party, goes onto a hill, and hears an old wolf singing toward the heavens.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The wolf addresses the man and gives him a root to powder, mix with clay, and snuff on the war-path to relieve fatigue.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The man asks the wolf for long life, promises always to smoke to him, and is told to spend the wolf's last night with him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "At sunrise the wolf dies crying to the sun, and the man cuts around the wolf's nose and down the back to make a strip he will wear on his scalp-lock in order to keep the wolf's spirit with him.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "After returning home, the man is often absent from the village, accompanies war parties in disguise, scouts ahead of others, and reports what he has seen at night.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "He captures many ponies and gives them to the leader; the returning party burns grass as a victory signal and paints their faces with charred grass.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Wolf Man and another leading scout say they never seem to tire; Wolf Man explains his power came from the wolf, and the other man says his own root was obtained from a horse in a dream.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Wolf Man dies of old age when a ray of sunlight rests on him, and his death is said to occur as the wolf died.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "In the second abstract, a man meets Coyote, smokes Coyote's pipe, is taken to Coyote's people, and is introduced there as Coyote's brother.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Coyotes roll in dust and give the man roots and medicines for hydrophobia and urinary troubles, and wolves roll in dust and give him a whistle whose blowing will cure sickness.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Other coyotes give the man a bone to kill people, a bone for a war club, and a piece of skull to wear on his forehead against bewitching; he returns home blowing the whistle and becomes a medicine-man.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
